/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:16:#     - Keep the original objects: 3-cell L arrows and 1/3-pixel axis-aligned walls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:18:#       the ray source (the arrow's right-angle vertex) to the grid center, nearest first.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:19:#     - Change 2 (D10): only static walls cause reflections, but a touched wall pixel is erased
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:20:#       from the output and removed from the live wall set for all later simulation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:23:#     - Example: arrow A near the center goes first, side-bounces off a teal wall at (7,8),
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:24:#       so output erases that wall pixel and A's later segment turns teal. Arrow B is farther
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:27:#       Original 142ca369 would keep the wall visible, would not erase the touched pixel,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:32:#     - Force one static-wall bounce on the center-near arrow so wall erasure is always visible.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:35:#     - Prefer a 3-pixel wall for the mandatory bounce so the erased center leaves a visible gap.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:39:#     - Original `wall_cells` was static. This is invalid because touched wall pixels disappear.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:40:#       The solver therefore keeps a mutable `live_walls` dict.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:45:#       the ray keeps its pre-bounce cell, while the wall pixel is erased and only subsequent
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:46:#       cells inherit the wall color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:47:#     - Original loop state omitted the wall configuration. This is invalid once walls disappear,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:48:#       so `wall_sig` is part of the visited state.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:50:#       input walls may flip direction; prior trails only terminate a later ray.
